{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: panel rewards assets whose recent risk is elevated vs their own history. Core legs: ts_z(kurt(60),250), ts_z(std(20),250), plus level legs cs_z(std(20)) and cs_z(kurt(120)). About 40 variants form a smooth plateau SR 1.6-1.96 across lookbacks, weights, and functional forms; delay-3 retains ~85 percent of SR so the effect decays slowly and should survive the 1-day lag OOS. Momentum, skew, beta legs add little or hurt. Reporting three weight variants of the validated core (4, 5, and 6 leg) rather than one spike plus fillers; train SR differences within the cluster are noise so expected mean OOS Sharpe is maximized by staying on the plateau.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:33:28.608443+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(add(add(cs_z(ts_z(kurt(60), 250)), cs_z(ts_z(std(20), 250))), cs_z(ts_z(std(20), 250))), add(add(cs_z(std(20)), cs_z(kurt(120))), cs_z(ts_z(kurt(60), 250))))", "add(add(add(cs_z(ts_z(kurt(60), 250)), cs_z(ts_z(std(20), 250))), cs_z(ts_z(std(20), 250))), add(cs_z(std(20)), cs_z(kurt(120))))", "add(add(cs_z(ts_z(kurt(60), 250)), cs_z(ts_z(std(20), 250))), add(cs_z(std(20)), cs_z(kurt(120))))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.9607, 1.9465, 1.932], "rationale": "All three are weight variants of one validated core: long assets whose 60d kurtosis and 20d volatility are high versus their own 250d history (ts_z legs) and high cross-sectionally in level (cs_z std(20) and kurt(120) legs). Family scan found kurt, std, beta strongest; refinement showed ts_z(.,250) timing roughly doubles the level-signal SR and the legs combine additively. Roughly 40 neighborhood variants form a smooth SR 1.6-1.96 plateau across lookbacks, weights and forms, and delay-3 keeps about 85 percent of SR, indicating slow decay and good expected OOS transfer; reported trio spans 4, 5 and 6 leg weightings of that plateau center (train SR 1.93-1.96, IC 0.008).", "n_batches_used": 8, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:33:37.566104+00:00"}
